@startuml Metrics & Monitoring Flow

skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

skinparam participant {
  BackgroundColor AliceBlue
  BorderColor SteelBlue
  FontStyle bold
}
skinparam database {
  BackgroundColor LemonChiffon
  BorderColor Goldenrod
}
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor DarkSlateGray
  LifeLineBorderColor SteelBlue
  GroupBorderColor Gray
  GroupBackgroundColor WhiteSmoke
  DividerBackgroundColor LightSteelBlue
  DividerFontStyle bold
  NoteBackgroundColor Cornsilk
  NoteBorderColor Goldenrod
}

title Metrics & Monitoring\n<size:11>Prometheus pull model  ·  Grafana dashboards</size>

box "Services  (namespace: e-learning-system)" #F0F8FF
  participant "auth-service\n:9090/metrics"     as s1
  participant "course-service\n:9090/metrics"   as s2
  participant "...\n:9090/metrics"              as sN
  participant "PostgreSQL\nexporter :9187"      as pg
end box

database    "Prometheus\n(TSDB)"               as prom
participant "Grafana"                          as graf
actor       "Developer / Ops"                  as user

note over s1, pg
  Each service registers metrics on startup via **promauto**:
  • **http_requests_total** {method, path, status_code}
  • **http_request_duration_seconds** {method, path, status_code}
  • **grpc_requests_total** {grpc_method, grpc_code}
  • **grpc_request_duration_seconds** {grpc_method, grpc_code}
  Exposed at **GET :9090/metrics** (Prometheus text format).
end note

== Scrape cycle (every ~15 s) ==

prom  ->  s1 : GET :9090/metrics
s1   --> prom : 200 OK · text/plain\n<size:9>(counter & histogram samples)</size>

prom  ->  s2 : GET :9090/metrics
s2   --> prom : 200 OK · text/plain

prom  ->  sN : GET :9090/metrics
sN   --> prom : 200 OK · text/plain

prom  ->  pg  : GET :9187/metrics
pg   --> prom : 200 OK · text/plain\n<size:9>(pg_up, pg_stat_* metrics)</size>

prom  ->  prom : store samples\nin local TSDB

== Dashboard query ==

user  ->  graf : open dashboard
graf  ->  prom : PromQL query\n<size:9>e.g. rate(http_requests_total[1m])</size>
prom --> graf  : time-series result
graf --> user  : rendered panel\n(graph / stat / table)

@enduml
